/// What every custom object has, whatever its category. The typed properties come from the generated `*Props`
/// modules; see the module of each category (`Unit.pkl`, `Hero.pkl`, ...).
abstract module moonwell.objects.Object

/// A value in `properties`: a scalar, a `List` of scalars (levels, or a comma-separated list), or a `List` of
/// `List<String>` (per-level lists).
typealias Value = Boolean|Number|String|List<Boolean|Number|String|List<String>>

/// The standard object this one copies, by its four-character id, such as `"hfoo"` (Footman).
base: String(length == 4)

/// The file this object is defined in, relative to `moonwell.pkl`. `Objects.merge` sets it; do not set it yourself.
source: String?

/// Fields without a typed property, keyed by friendly name or by field rawcode, such as
/// `["amountHealedOrDamaged"] = List(200, 400, 600)` on a Holy Light copy. The CLI checks the key, the value and
/// whether the field applies to `base`. `null` inherits from the base.
properties: Mapping<String, Value?> = new {}
